  "body": "We had a discussion recently more or less along the lines of 'modules shouldn't know about `SynapseError`s (except for use with their own web resources)', but I just noticed that the `on_create_room` callback encourages/requires doing it that way.\r\n\r\nShould we add an alternative? (e.g.: `return False, \"failure message\"`?)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/5e0e6835416776e4d938f53b3c9a005970f88127/docs/modules/third_party_rules_callbacks.md?plain=1#L68-L69",
